<title>AUSTRIA: Slovenia PM hopes for EU membership by 2002.</title>
<headline>Slovenia PM hopes for EU membership by 2002.</headline>
<dateline>SALZBURG, Austria 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slovenia is expecting to begin membership talks with the European Union (EU) in 1998 and hopes to join the 15-nation bloc by 2002, Prime Minister Janez Drnovsek said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;It's difficult to forecast when (EU) enlargement will take place. I think Slovenia will be ready before 2002 but I am confident negotiations will start in the beginning of 1998,&quot; Drnovsek told a news conference at the Second Central and Eastern European Summit in Salzburg.</p>
<p>Earlier in the day, a senior official from the European Commission said it had agreed in principle to recommend the EU open entry talks with Poland, Hungary, the Czech Republic, Slovenia, Estonia and Cyprus.</p>
